                        "review": "At first glance, Super Mega Space Blaster Special Turbo appears to be an average space shooter. It is in fact much more than that. It has a good variety of game modes each with their own individual mechanics. The game is fun and reminds me of many retro games. \n\nSuper Mega Space Blaster Special Turbo becomes addictive quite quickly and is a lot of fun to play in local co-op as well. The game improves on the original in all areas and the new ‘Save the Colony’ mode brings new challenges. The game has that ‘just one more go’ feeling. \n\nThe ship list is vast with 15 space blasters to unlock. Each space blaster has different stats meaning there is something for everyone. Being able to upgrade power-ups and buy perks in the shop is a great addition too and really helps on long score-chasing runs.\n\nPros:\n•\tAddictive, challenging gameplay\n•\tGreat variety of ships\n•\tUpgrade shop\n•\tAmazing soundtrack\n•\tVaried game-modes\n•\tLocal co-op\n•\tReal arcade retro shooter feel\n\nCons:\n•\tSimple story\n•\tSimple graphics (although they do have a hand-drawn charm)\n•\tFont choice (can be difficult to read at lower resolutions)\n\nOverall, Super Mega Space Blaster Special Turbo is worth the price. It offers hours of retro space shooting action and some fun challenges. I haven’t played a game that filled me with nostalgia this much since Geometry Wars. I highly recommend the game and give it 8.5 out of 10.",
